{"agent":"recover-3h","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`on_refutation` still returns None for a gate whose recorded outcome is `passed`. The docstring in the same function defines None as “passed by a clean review, or not passed”, so a caller that only adds the “ON REFUTATION” suffix when this returns a dict now renders a plain pass. Input: `gates[gate].outcome == \"passed\"`, `evidence[\"passed_on_refutation\"] == {\"confirmed\": 0}`, and `triage_counts` reports `confirmed == 1` (the B31e91454f8 state, including a status read that does not re-enter triage). The new branch returns None while the record stays passed, so the gate still shows passed — and the refutation flag that made the bad pass visible is suppressed. Revocation lives only in `_revoke_refutation_pass`, which this read path never calls, and the new regression test never calls `on_refutation`.","digest":"afe78514f6f1c8be","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/gates/outcomes.py:211","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/gates/outcomes.py:211"}],"chunks_total":1,"combined_gates":["rubber_duck","critic"],"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":5683,"diff_sha":"773f4cc4cbc4c1aa2e66e29419a4ef398a6f2eae128056ddb574cec431a7bf4d","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B31e91454f8","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":288.2,"family":"xai","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"7186a0a90c983b47","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B31e91454f8.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261108T230854Z-c95bd5cf.jsonl","reason":"","review_degraded":[{"at":1794179334.5609682,"family":"google","gate":"rubber_duck","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","reason":"HTTP 429","reviewer":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite"}],"review_id":"ff2ad9d43e62","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"b5c8b866bfe46ffc04dac